WEBVTT

00:08:57.367 --> 00:09:00.131
People gravitate toward
their existing friends and groups,

00:09:00.155 --> 00:09:01.808
leaving fault lines intact.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.686
And even if you overcome that barrier,

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.476
happy hour is not set up
for meaningful connection.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.593
Group conversations tend to stay shallow.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.746
What people need to defeat loneliness
is a deeper connection.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.462
And that's more likely to come
through talking one-on-one

00:09:16.486 --> 00:09:19.096
or through actually
doing something together.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.148
For example, there's a digital
marketing company, Bazaarvoice,

00:09:22.172 --> 00:09:25.046
that has an onboarding process
lasting a few days.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.529
Newcomers get to know their colleagues
through problem-solving activities

00:09:28.553 --> 00:09:29.739
that create connection,

00:09:29.763 --> 00:09:31.046
like scavenger hunts.